;; Java writes two digits where one would do (types §2.12, Decided
;; 2026-10-01): the smallest double is 4.9E-324 in the dump and `5e-324`
;; in the printer, whose Rust layout wants the one digit again. Every
;; subnormal whose spelling is one digit, in both signs: the interval of
;; the smallest ones holds several one-digit decimals (5e-324 reads back
;; with 3e-324 to 7e-324), 9.88e-324 rounds up into the next decade.
5e-324 -5e-324 1e-323 -1e-323 1.5e-323 -1.5e-323
4.94065645841246544e-324 9.8813129168249309e-324 3e-324 7e-324
2e-323 3e-323 4.9e-323 5e-323 -5e-323 5.9e-323 6e-323 7e-323 9e-323
1e-322 1.5e-322 2.2250738585072014e-308 2.225073858507201e-308
